   Example:     Asked for Sanskrit → gives "rāmo'sti" instead
                of "रामोऽस्ति"
   Root Cause:  Both representations exist in training data;
                model conflates them without explicit script
                direction.
   Mitigation:  Add explicit "Write in Devanagari script"
                instructions; add script-specific training pairs.

2. SANDHI DECOMPOSITION ERRORS
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Description: Model fails to correctly apply/reverse sandhi
                rules in translation.
   Example:     'देवेन्द्र' → "deva + indra" not recognised
                as compound; translated word-by-word incorrectly.
   Root Cause:  Sandhi creates unseen token sequences;
                small model has insufficient capacity.
   Mitigation:  Include sandhi-split pairs in training data;
                use a model with Sanskrit-aware tokenizer.

3. CASE ENDING CONFUSION
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Description: Model confuses subject/object/instrument roles
                in translation due to misidentified vibhakti.
   Example:     "रामेण" (by Rama) → translated as "to Rama"
                (confusing instrumental with dative).
   Root Cause:  Vibhakti suffixes are subtle; model lacks
                sufficient morphological examples.
   Mitigation:  Expand grammar training examples for all 8
                vibhaktis across multiple noun stems.

4. HALLUCINATED VERSE ATTRIBUTION
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Description: Model attributes a verse to the wrong text
                (e.g., says a Mahabharata verse is from Rigveda).
   Example:     "सत्यमेव जयते" → incorrectly cited as
                from Bhagavad Gita instead of Mundaka Upanishad.
   Root Cause:  Limited factual grounding; causal LM optimises
                for fluency, not factual accuracy.
   Mitigation:  Add retrieval augmentation (RAG) over a Sanskrit
                corpus; use Constitutional AI / RLHF.

5. INCOMPLETE GENERATION
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Description: Model truncates output mid-sentence for longer
                explanations.
   Example:     Explaining Bhagavad Gita → cuts off after 2
                of 3 intended points.
   Root Cause:  MAX_NEW_TOKENS=256 cap; small model (1B param)
                struggles with long coherent generation.
   Mitigation:  Increase max_new_tokens; use larger base model;
                add length-control tokens in instruction.
""")

