We successfully fine-tuned a 1B-parameter LLM on a curated
Sanskrit–English instruction dataset using QLoRA on a single
T4 GPU. The fine-tuned model shows measurable improvement on
translation, explanation, and grammar Q&A tasks compared to
the base model, demonstrating that even small datasets (150–250
carefully crafted examples) can induce domain-specific behaviour
through instruction tuning. The primary bottleneck is the
tokenizer/vocab mismatch and data volume, not the fine-tuning
methodology itself.
